{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793344795,"nonce":"zF6cKR3Spgh2VAYjsSdmD65F5B0=","title":"Retain bound-method receivers through closure use","message":"Native AOT execution of AotOptimizationCalls binds receiver.apply, reads receiver.score, then invokes the method in a loop. At all existing MIR optimization levels the HIR drop analysis emits free(receiver) after the getter, before the bound closure is invoked. Its virtual-dispatch header is then read from freed storage.\n\nThe HIR closure-capture pre-scan visits MethodReference receivers without recording their variables as captures, while MIR lowering actually constructs MakeClosure(thunk, receiver). Treat bound receiver storage as captured just like ordinary lambda captures, including field, index and cast receiver expressions. Preserve the ordinary escaping-expression traversal.\n\nReproducer and before/after evidence are kept in ~/rayzor-aot-audit-20261030 on the NUC: call-probes.json, call-probes/lifetime-mir.log and the AotOptimizationCalls regression fixture. Validate both closure retention analysis and native execution across MIR/LLVM/codegen combinations.","files":null}]}